# Firefox Extension Conventions

## Manifest

- MV2 only — not MV3. LISD machines run Firefox, and MV2 is the correct target.
- Required permissions: `tabs`, `downloads`, `storage`, `http://ims.lisd.net/*`, `http://localhost:4321/*`
- No extra permissions without explicit instruction

## WebSocket Connection (background.js)

- Connect to `ws://localhost:4321/ws` on install and maintain the connection
- Reconnect with exponential backoff on disconnect — max 5 retries, then surface error to relay
- All messages are JSON: `{ "type": "command_name", "payload": { ... } }`
- Never use `chrome.*` APIs — use `browser.*` (Firefox WebExtension API)

## DOM Automation (content.js)

All DOM interactions must use explicit waits, never `setTimeout` for sequencing.

Use this pattern for waiting on elements:
```javascript
function waitForElement(selector, timeoutMs = 10000) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const existing = document.querySelector(selector);
    if (existing) return resolve(existing);
    const observer = new MutationObserver(() => {
      const el = document.querySelector(selector);
      if (el) { observer.disconnect(); resolve(el); }
    });
    observer.observe(document.body, { childList: true, subtree: true });
    setTimeout(() => { observer.disconnect(); reject(new Error(`Timeout waiting for: ${selector}`)); }, timeoutMs);
  });
}
```

Every automation step has a 10-second timeout. On timeout, send a failure message back to the relay with the step name and selector that failed.

## Selector Strategy

- Prefer `data-*` attributes and stable IDs over positional or class-based selectors
- Never use nth-child or sibling combinators for navigation — i3 DOM structure will change
- If no stable attribute exists, use the innerText of a button/label as the selector signal, not its position
- Comment every selector with why it was chosen: `// data-testid="site-filter" — stable across i3 versions`

## File Download Watcher

- Watch `C:\Users\[username]\Downloads` for files matching `report*.csv` (glob, not exact match)
- Handle increment suffix: `report (1).csv`, `report (2).csv` — match the most recently modified file
- Read file contents, send to relay, then signal completion
- Never hardcode the username — resolve it dynamically: `navigator.userAgent` won't work; the background script must use `browser.downloads.search` to find the download path

## Error Reporting

Every error sent back to the relay uses this shape:
```json
{ "type": "error", "step": "step_name", "message": "plain English description" }
```

Never swallow errors silently. Every step that can fail must have a catch block that reports back.
